# USE flags for the 'zero' board profile. 'xarm setup'/'xarm tune' copy this
# into the shared arm64 sysroot as package.use/xprofile-zero.use.

# sys-kernel/linux-firmware installs 2.0 GB by default -- more than the whole
# zero image. savedconfig cuts that to the ~108 KB this board actually needs
# (see savedconfig/sys-kernel/linux-firmware).
#
#   savedconfig    honour the keep-list; without it the emerge is 2.0 GB
#   -deduplicate   REQUIRED_USE forbids it together with savedconfig
#   -initramfs     default-on, and wrong here twice over: it builds an AMD
#                  microcode image (there is no AMD CPU on a BCM2837) and it
#                  arms mount-boot_pkg_preinst, which insists on a mounted
#                  /boot -- fatal in a cross emerge with --root=
#   -compress-*    default-off, pinned so a global USE cannot turn it on:
#                  sys-kernel/raspberrypi-image ships no .config, so whether
#                  the prebuilt kernel has FW_LOADER_COMPRESS_XZ cannot be
#                  checked here, and a compressed mt7662.bin that the loader
#                  cannot decompress fails at request_firmware() time -- on
#                  the board, not in the build
sys-kernel/linux-firmware savedconfig -deduplicate -initramfs -compress-xz -compress-zstd
